=================================== RULINGS ====================================

R1 (disclosed deviation — the literal vs the import): ACCEPTED. TS7016 verified by measurement (§7), not taken
   on the builder's word. The deviation is disclosed at the line with its reason. Its residual cost is A1.

R2 (disclosed deviation — tick.test.ts, one line outside the owned files): ACCEPTED, and CREDITED. It is the
   exception acceptance 2 anticipated in terms, the smallest possible fix, disclosed at the line, and §3 proves
   both that the sentinel caught it and that nothing else could have.

R3 (the 1-in-7 flake, left unfixed): ACCEPTED as out of scope. It is upstream of scripts/no-vendor.test.mjs by
   the builder's diagnosis and by everything I measured; it did not reproduce in 6 runs + bisellium ci; and the
   builder did not mask it — `result.status ?? 1` is unchanged and the signal is now named. Disclosure was honest.
   It remains UNREFUTED (0/6 is compatible with p up to ~0.39); it is a successor's target, not this opus's.

R4 (the 2s->8s widening): HONEST HEADROOM, and strictly strengthening — not flake-masking. Reasoning and the
   live proof are in §5. A shorter deadline is the weaker assertion here, not the stronger one.

R5 (the retitle amendment's provenance): D-021-CLEAN. D-021 assigns ownership by REF, not by sella — "while
   opus/<id> exists, only a checkout on opus/<id> writes the record" — and the amendment landed in e52f64a on
   opus/W-072. `--sella architect` is an unverified declaration, but it is corroborated by an independent artifact
   on the same tree: the brief's Sequence prescribes that exact invocation with that exact --reason, and the brief
   is the architect's signed document (rev 4, finding 15). One amendments entry, one field, superseded title intact.

R6 (acceptance 4's promise, held against the mechanism as the brief demands): the mechanism DELIVERS it. §3 shows
   the motivating shape — a bare vendor name resolved against the inherited PATH — caught, fail-closed, and
   attributed to the offending test file by name. The narrowing is a boundary, not an evasion. B1 and B2 do not
   touch the promise's scope; they are holes in what KEEPS it true.

VERDICT: FAIL (round 1). Two blocking, both one-line-to-one-row remedies, both on the same theme the brief spent
five revisions on: the fail-closed guarantee's own guards. Everything else measured clean, and the opus has
already earned its keep — it found a real five-spawn vendor-contact defect that the existing suite reported green.
